# BUGS

Only the linear and u-interleaved layouts of the uncompressed 8-bit formats are made, and only two-dimensional textures with plane descriptors of one plane; no cube, 3D or multisampled descriptors, no mip-level selection in the sampler beyond the limits, and no anisotropy or depth comparison.
Whether the render target descriptor's sRGB bit is also set for an sRGB colour target is not established: the tile buffer is taken to hold the encoded bytes, and the bit to encode again on writeback, so it is left clear.
The border colour is stored as the caller gives it; whether it is before or after the texture's swizzle is not established.
The constant of the first fixed-function target is the only one the hardware reads (the other descriptors' are ignored): the recipe's caller gives every descriptor the same constant, and a target whose constant differs needs a blend shader.
The Load Destination bit is set as the specification says; whether it also loads the target from memory at the start of a pass that clears it is not established.
